# WHAT THE IMAGE BUILD MUST NOT CARRY. `server/Dockerfile` does `COPY . .`, so everything here is
# sent to the daemon on every build, and a checkout that has built once holds hundreds of megabytes
# of `build/` directories against a few tens of megabytes of sources. CI never notices — a fresh
# checkout has none of them — which is why this file is easy to forget and only bites locally.
#
# NOTHING GIT TRACKS MAY BE LISTED HERE. The build context is a working tree as far as git is
# concerned, and the `io.github.youndie.kore.build` plugin runs git in it to decide the `dirty` flag
# it compiles into `/version`; an excluded tracked file reads as a deleted one and the stamp becomes
# `-dirty` for ever. katcher published exactly that. So this list is only what git ignores anyway.
#
# `.git` IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT: without it the commit in `/version` is `unknown`.
**/build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
.idea/
local.properties
